        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mryk92xw8yrf4inx",
          "message": {
            "text": "Two-tier safety, deliberately asymmetric. The **in-flight** guard (`c.inFlight === 0`) is HARD — applied in every mode, never dropped — because closing a cluster with a running query rejects the caller's promise. The **recency** guard (`minIdleMs`) is SOFT — cap/idle honor it to avoid churn-evicting a just-touched cluster, but the headroom mode DROPS it: under memory pressure a reopen is cheaper than an OOM. Losing this distinction (e.g. making headroom respect recency) would let `external` reach the ceiling during a large cross-project fan-out with nothing evictable.",
            "markdown": "Two-tier safety, deliberately asymmetric. The **in-flight** guard (`c.inFlight === 0`) is HARD — applied in every mode, never dropped — because closing a cluster with a running query rejects the caller's promise. The **recency** guard (`minIdleMs`) is SOFT — cap/idle honor it to avoid churn-evicting a just-touched cluster, but the headroom mode DROPS it: under memory pressure a reopen is cheaper than an OOM. Losing this distinction (e.g. making headroom respect recency) would let `external` reach the ceiling during a large cross-project fan-out with nothing evictable."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/db/clusterEviction.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 95,
                  "endLine": 113,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    return evictable\n      .filter((c) => input.now - c.lastAccess >= input.idleMs)\n      .map((c) => c.dbPath);\n  }\n\n  // cap + headroom both evict in LRU order (oldest access first).\n  const byLru = [...evictable].sort((a, b) => a.lastAccess - b.lastAccess);\n\n  if (input.mode === 'cap') {\n    const overBy = input.clusters.length - input.maxOpen;\n    if (overBy <= 0) return [];\n    // Only evict clusters aged past the recency guard, so a burst that opened\n    // many clusters at once doesn't immediately churn-evict a just-touched one.\n    const aged = byLru.filter((c) => input.now - c.lastAccess >= input.minIdleMs);\n    return aged.slice(0, overBy).map((c) => c.dbPath);\n  }\n\n  // headroom (critical): free `targetEvictions` LRU clusters, dropping the\n  // recency guard (memory pressure outweighs a reopen) but NEVER the in-flight"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
